  "worked_solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=-2i+0j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=3i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j)-(-2i+0j) \\\\  & =5i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
